{"id": "65a9e5eedd30dc2e18ea910dff59eaa2", "text": "also means one without beginning. Dividing the word anadi  as ana and adi \nleads to two interpretations.  Ana means activ ity, adi is beginning, so anadi  \nmeans the one who is the cause of activity in everyone. Also, ana means \nthe deity mukhya prana (vayudeva)  and hence anadi  can also be interpreted \nas the one who existed even before  the deity mukhya prana . This \ninterpretation  is also consistent with the Vedic quote in  the Purusha", "embedding": [0.011998742818832397, 0.01893478073179722, -0.023849090561270714, 0.05186839401721954, 0.058635611087083817, -0.050543397665023804, 0.08039066195487976, -0.028993410989642143, 0.04073508083820343, 0.038033273071050644, 0.03443523123860359, -0.07977235317230225, 0.031868163496255875, -0.03740498423576355, 0.0192406065762043, 0.04496544599533081, -0.0821596011519432, -0.05499023199081421, 0.005053255707025528, -0.000402227247832343, 0.0628352165222168, 0.06263336539268494, -0.041762616485357285, 0.04649001732468605, -0.014376480132341385, 0.0027196689043194056, -0.02325764112174511, -0.04570818692445755, -0.015901105478405952, 0.03284336254000664, -0.03642316907644272, -0.03960060700774193, 0.1503172665834427, 0.04594269022345543, -0.029882026836276054, 0.04669324681162834, 0.009718021377921104, 0.061261504888534546, -0.03171682730317116, -0.04263872653245926, -0.015833277255296707, -0.01840522512793541, -0.041185569018125534, -0.06950655579566956, -0.04155372828245163, -0.03394724801182747, -0.029414203017950058, 0.03230299428105354, 0.0004895124584436417, 0.04262387752532959, 0.012728855013847351, 0.022996291518211365, -0.05941246077418327, 0.03296423703432083, 0.04047645255923271, -0.012614944018423557, -0.020460497587919235, -0.023000797256827354, -0.04064209759235382, -0.0537598580121994, -0.019845010712742805, 0.04860358685255051, 0.03673302382230759, -0.026046784594655037, 0.07870840281248093, -0.11632009595632553, 0.04700610414147377, -0.08075405657291